{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"94d545db3cab29d4","name":"card_event_strong_bond","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/BrothersInArms/events/card_event_strong_bond","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"STRONG BOND","text":"Friendly ground unit gets Guard and: \"Add a US 3-cost unit to your support line at the start of your turn.\"","flavorText":"After the American Revolution in 1783 the UK recognized American independence and the two countries established diplomatic relations in 1785. Ever since the UK and the US have remained close partners. The UK-US relations at the start of WWII were complex as the Americans were divided on what the role of the nation should be in the war, or if it should interfere at all. However, public opinion changed, especially during the Battle of Britain, as it showed that the German war machine was not invincible, and by April 1941 a public poll showed that the majority of Americans were in favor of joining the war against the Axis. Finally the Japanese attack on Pearl Harbor on December 7, 1941, ended the debate once and for all and shortly after the US was at war with the Axis powers.","faction":"Britain","type":"order","rarity":"Common","cost":4,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_strong_bond","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_strong_bond_title","SourceString":"STRONG BOND","LocalizedString":"STRONG BOND"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_strong_bond_text","SourceString":"Friendly ground unit gets Guard and: \"Add a US 3-cost unit to your support line at the start of your turn.\"","LocalizedString":"Friendly ground unit gets Guard and: \"Add a US 3-cost unit to your support line at the start of your turn.\""},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_strong_bond_history","SourceString":"After the American Revolution in 1783 the UK recognized American independence and the two countries established diplomatic relations in 1785. Ever since the UK and the US have remained close partners. The UK-US relations at the start of WWII were complex as the Americans were divided on what the role of the nation should be in the war, or if it should interfere at all. However, public opinion changed, especially during the Battle of Britain, as it showed that the German war machine was not invincible, and by April 1941 a public poll showed that the majority of Americans were in favor of joining the war against the Axis. Finally the Japanese attack on Pearl Harbor on December 7, 1941, ended the debate once and for all and shortly after the US was at war with the Axis powers.","LocalizedString":"After the American Revolution in 1783 the UK recognized American independence and the two countries established diplomatic relations in 1785. Ever since the UK and the US have remained close partners. The UK-US relations at the start of WWII were complex as the Americans were divided on what the role of the nation should be in the war, or if it should interfere at all. However, public opinion changed, especially during the Battle of Britain, as it showed that the German war machine was not invincible, and by April 1941 a public poll showed that the majority of Americans were in favor of joining the war against the Axis. Finally the Japanese attack on Pearl Harbor on December 7, 1941, ended the debate once and for all and shortly after the US was at war with the Axis powers."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BrothersInArms","isReserved":true,"usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnStartofTurn","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardReset"],"draftBaseWeight":0.8,"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Monty_17'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Misc/OrdersFeb17/Monty_17.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/USA/Candid